# CQ 24: Which values does a quality of service carry, for which parameter and
# in which unit?
#
# Clause 5.5.5 characterises a communication by parameters, and the value is
# reified so that it can carry the parameter it belongs to alongside the
# quantity and the unit. Without that reification a model could state a number
# and not what it is a number of.
#
# forParameter is functional: one value quantifies one parameter, which
# negative model 03 tests.
#
# Test cases 1 and 3 state three values, case 4 two. Reading them across the
# cases shows what changes with the transmission mode, and question 27
# compares them per parameter.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
SELECT ?communication ?parameter ?quantity ?unit
WHERE {
  ?communication iso7498:hasQualityOfService ?qos .
  ?qos iso7498:hasValue ?v .
  ?v iso7498:forParameter ?p .
  OPTIONAL { ?v iso7498:quantity ?quantity }
  OPTIONAL { ?v iso7498:unit     ?unit }
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?p), ".*#", "") AS ?parameter)
} ORDER BY ?communication ?parameter
